      "message": "The deferral logic and adding `.noFields()` to the query are great and definitely needed.\n\nHowever, subclassing `PrivateInternals_BooleanCondition.SubclassOnlyInCoreServer` directly inside a REST handler is an anti-pattern. That class is explicitly documented as `DO NOT USE`, and only exists as internal plumbing for `PermissionBackendCondition`.\n\nCould we instead add a first-class factory method to `BooleanCondition` (e.g. `BooleanCondition.lazy(BooleanSupplier)` or `fromSupplier` in `com.google.gerrit.extensions.conditions.BooleanCondition`)?\n\nThat way:\n1. `BooleanCondition` gets a clean, reusable lazy evaluation mechanism for all actions/plugins.\n2. Here we can simply write:\n   `and(testCond(REVERT), BooleanCondition.lazy(() -\u003e isChangePartOfSubmission(change.getSubmissionId())))`\n3. We avoid the 18 lines of anonymous inner class boilerplate and keep `PrivateInternals_*` internal.\n\nAlso, `isChangePartOfSubmission` below can return primitive `boolean` instead of boxed `Boolean`.",
